From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cmatte <cmatte@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let the broker's acl_file decide after an ACL grant

On Mosquitto 2.1 the ACL check runs through every registered plugin
callback in order and stops at the first result that is not
MOSQ_ERR_PLUGIN_DEFER or MOSQ_ERR_PLUGIN_IGNORE. The broker's own
acl_file check is registered after the plugins, so when go-auth grants
access with MOSQ_ERR_SUCCESS the acl_file is never consulted.

Return MOSQ_ERR_PLUGIN_IGNORE for a grant instead, so a configured
acl_file can still restrict access. Without an acl_file every callback
ignores and the broker allows the request, as before. Denials and
errors are unchanged. Building against Mosquitto older than 2.1 (or
without its version macro) fails with #error instead of silently
falling back to ending the check on a grant.
---
 auth-plugin.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/auth-plugin.c b/auth-plugin.c
index fc45f26..35dfa00 100644
--- a/auth-plugin.c
+++ b/auth-plugin.c
@@ -14,6 +14,12 @@
 
 #include "go-auth.h"
 
+/* An ACL grant returns MOSQ_ERR_PLUGIN_IGNORE, which needs Mosquitto 2.1+.
+ * Fail the build rather than fall back to ending the check on a grant. */
+#if !defined(LIBMOSQUITTO_VERSION_NUMBER) || LIBMOSQUITTO_VERSION_NUMBER < 2001000
+# error "Returning MOSQ_ERR_PLUGIN_IGNORE needs Mosquitto 2.1 or later"
+#endif
+
 // Same constant as one in go-auth.go.
 #define AuthRejected 0
 #define AuthGranted 1
@@ -133,7 +139,9 @@ int mosquitto_auth_acl_check(void *userdata, const char *clientid, const char *u
   switch (ret)
   {
   case AuthGranted:
-    return MOSQ_ERR_SUCCESS;
+    /* A grant does not end the check; later checks (e.g. the broker's
+     * own acl_file) still decide. */
+    return MOSQ_ERR_PLUGIN_IGNORE;
     break;
   case AuthRejected:
     return MOSQ_ERR_ACL_DENIED;
